      "id": "borax-pentaborate-pds-2024",
      "type": "handbook",
      "reference": "U.S. Borax, Ammonium Pentaborate Product Data Sheet, September 2024. https://www.borax.com/BoraxCorp/media/Borax-Main/Resources/Data-Sheets/ammonium-pentaborate.pdf?ext=.pdf",
      "used_for": "Pages 1–3: whole tetrahydrate product, ammonia/water/boric-acid reaction, crystalline supply state, moisture sensitivity, decomposition and container examples. Theoretical oxide composition, solubility and producer examples are not inventory factors or operating instructions."
    },
    {
      "id": "borax-pentaborate-spec-v3",
      "type": "handbook",
      "reference": "Borax Français S.A.S., Ammonium Pentaborate Technical Powder, BFC31-v.3, undated. https://www.borax.com/BoraxCorp/media/Borax-Main/Resources/Specifications-Sheets/ammonium-pentaborate-technical-powder.pdf?ext=.pdf",
      "used_for": "Complete single page: manufactured crystalline tetrahydrate and producer analytical specifications. Equivalent tetrahydrate assay can exceed 100%; it is not a physical constituent mass fraction, yield, dry-salt fraction or universal grade."
    },
    {
      "id": "borax-pentaborate-sds-2025",
      "type": "handbook",
      "reference": "Rio Tinto Borates / Borax Français S.A.S., Ammonium Pentaborate SDS AP-BF-AP-EN, January 2025. https://sds.riotinto.com/display/rtm/FileName-502775",
      "used_for": "Complete 7-page SDS: sections 1, 3, 9 and 15 connect the named whole tetrahydrate product, CAS 12046-04-7, >99.0% content and the separate anhydrous inventory number 12007-89-5. Sections 6–13 support dust, moisture, ammonia and water-release assessment. No occupational limit, toxicity endpoint or theoretical conversion is an LCI default."
    },
    {
      "id": "dmcc-pentaborate-product",
      "type": "handbook",
      "reference": "DMCC Speciality Chemicals, Ammonium Pentaborate product page, undated. https://dmcc.com/product/boron-chemicals/ammonium-pentaborate",
      "used_for": "Independent producer product context: CAS 12046-04-7, diammonium decaborate octahydrate formula and HDPE-bag supply. The doubled formula denotes the same hydrate composition; no double product mass. The displayed ammonium-oxide label contains a Na4 typo and is not used quantitatively. No factory recipe, yield or fuel mix is established."
    },
    {
      "id": "ec-pef-multifunctionality-2021",
      "type": "official_guidance",
      "reference": "European Commission, Recommendation C(2021) 9332 final, Annexes 1–2, 2021. https://environment.ec.europa.eu/system/files/2021-12/Annexes%201%20to%202.pdf",
      "used_for": "Section 4.5, PDF pages 63–64: investigate subdivision/system expansion, then relevant physical relationships and justified alternatives for multifunctionality. General method only; no borate-specific allocation percentage or substitution credit."
    }
  ],
