          "comments": [
            {
              "#text": "Boric acid is a water-soluble white compound that occurs naturally. It consists of oxygen, boron, and hydrogen. It has antifungal and antimicrobial properties. It is usually encountered as colorless crystals or a white powder, that dissolves in water, and occurs in nature as the mineral sassolite. It is a weak acid with antiviral, antifungal, and antiseptic properties. It is soluble in water and does not have any characteristic odour.",
              "@xml:lang": "en"
            },
            {
              "#text": "硼酸是一种可溶于水的白色化合物，自然存在。它由氧、硼和氢组成。它具有抗真菌和抗微生物的特性。它通常以无色晶体或白色粉末的形式出现，可以溶于水，在自然界中以矿物萨索莱特的形式存在。它是一种具有抗病毒、抗真菌和防腐性质的弱酸。它可以溶于水，没有任何特征性的气味。",
              "@xml:lang": "zh"
            }
          ],
